# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere, including Windows checkouts.
#
# This is not cosmetic here. tools/stamp-sw.js derives the service-worker cache name from a hash
# of each precached file's bytes, so a checkout that swapped LF for CRLF would compute a different
# stamp from the one committed — `stamp-sw.js --check` would fail on a fresh clone, and GitHub
# Pages would serve bytes that don't match what the stamp was calculated over. Pinning eol=lf
# keeps the hash reproducible across machines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Sources git should never touch.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
